# Firehorse Skillful Report — Carbon Footprint Report

**Report type:** EN 15978 Carbon Footprint Report
**Agent:** `src/firehorse/report-module.ts` (format: `carbon-footprint`)
**Feeds from:** `src/agents/material-oracle.agent.ts` (embodied carbon per material)
**CLI:** `dws firehorse-report --format carbon-footprint --input '{"organizationId":"org-1","industry":"construction","periodStart":"2025-01-01","periodEnd":"2025-12-31"}'`
**API:** `POST /api/v1/firehorse/reports/generate` with `{"format":"carbon-footprint","organizationId":"...","industry":"...","periodStart":"...","periodEnd":"..."}`

## What This Skill Knows

EN 15978 lifecycle carbon assessment for construction projects. The definitive tool for EPBD compliance (embodied carbon >1,000m² buildings mandatory by 2028) and CSRD E1 climate disclosures.

**Proof point:** In a 5-hour session, DWS IQ calculated 420 kgCO2e/m² for a hybrid concrete-timber office tower in Helsinki using real NCC project data. That's the bar.

## Report Structure

### Section 1: Project Summary

- Building type, gross floor area (GFA), location
- Reference study period
- Overall carbon intensity: X kgCO2e/m²
- Benchmark comparison (Finnish/Nordic industry average)

### Section 2: Lifecycle Stage Breakdown

| Stage | Label             | kgCO2e | % of total |
| ----- | ----------------- | ------ | ---------- |
| A1–A3 | Product stage     | —      | —          |
| A4    | Transport to site | —      | —          |
| A5    | Construction      | —      | —          |
| B1–B7 | Use stage         | —      | —          |
| C1–C4 | End of life       | —      | —          |
| D     | Beyond boundary   | —      | —          |

### Section 3: Material Breakdown

Top 10 materials by carbon contribution, each with:

- Emission factor (kgCO2e/unit, source: ICE v3 or EC3 EPD)
- Quantity and unit
- Lower-carbon alternative with saving estimate

### Section 4: CBAM Implications

If project imports Annex I materials (steel, aluminium, cement), calculates:

- Carbon intensity of imported goods
- CBAM certificate requirement estimate
- Border adjustment cost at €65/tCO2e

### Section 5: Improvement Pathway

- Priority material substitutions (ranked by saving/cost ratio)
- Target carbon intensity reduction (e.g. -30% via recycled steel + low-carbon concrete)
- Projected cost impact

## Benchmark Data

| Building type         | Nordic avg (kgCO2e/m²) | Source                                          |
| --------------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| Office (concrete)     | 400–600                | Finnish Carbon Footprint Calculation Guide 2023 |
| Residential (timber)  | 150–250                | RT 20-11395                                     |
| Industrial hall       | 200–350                | EN 15978 EPD database                           |
| Proof point (DWS/NCC) | 420                    | DWS IQ BIM pipeline, Feb 2026                   |

## Output Format

```json
{
  "format": "carbon-footprint",
  "project": "string",
  "grossFloorArea": number,
  "carbonIntensity": number,
  "unit": "kgCO2e/m2",
  "stageBreakdown": { "A1-A3": number, "A4": number, "A5": number, "B": number, "C": number, "D": number },
  "materialBreakdown": [{ "material": "", "kgCO2e": number, "factor": number, "source": "" }],
  "cbamImplications": { "applicable": boolean, "certificateEstimate": number },
  "improvementPathway": [{ "action": "", "savingKgCO2e": number, "savingPercent": number }],
  "markdown": "full report as markdown",
  "epbdCompliant": boolean
}
```

## Standards References

- EN 15978:2011 — Assessment of environmental performance of buildings
- EN 15804:2012+A2:2019 — EPD core rules for construction products
- ICE Database v3.0 — Inventory of Carbon and Energy
- EC3 (Carbon Calculator for Construction) — EPD database
- EPBD (EU Directive 2024/1275) — embodied carbon for new buildings >1,000m² by 2028
- Finnish Carbon Footprint Calculation Guide (RT 20-11395)
- ISO 14040/14044 — LCA principles
